fees as a condition of development approval.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"5db047ae-f3d7-584e-b483-e8239e92815f"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"12.55.050","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/12.55.050","content_hash":"a39eab926d459e33cdb60b1eaa34b686c1fb500203ecfa572d8bf5d55bf0d1ac","heading":null,"ordinal":6,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:12.55.050:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:12.55.050:block:6","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/12.55.050","text":"“New development” or “development project” means and includes any project undertaken for the purpose of development, including without limitation a project involving the issuance of a permit for construction, reconstruction, or change of use, but not a project involving the issuance of a permit to operate or to remodel, rehabilitate, or improve an existing structure, nor the rebuilding of a structure destroyed or damaged by an act of God.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"fbae9388-8fe5-5015-9568-66f35754ad93"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"12.55.050","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/12.55.050","content_hash":"a1b524387497b741b25b5bb44ce0cccbdea5ef08237455d83fbc8dfc80ed1de0","heading":null,"ordinal":7,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:12.55.050:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:12.55.050:block:7","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/12.55.050","text":"“Nonresidential development project” means all development other than residential development projects.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"dbf5af76-ca7c-5925-a59e-2ec951befb92"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"12.55.050","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/12.55.050","content_hash":"eea